// The resumed run's overlay, applied by gate.sh to `resumed` alone, after
// gate.config:
//   nextflow run . -c gate/gate.config -name resumed -resume <cold's session> -c gate/resume.config
//
// The output DSL defaults to overwrite 'standard', which compares a source and
// its target by name, size and mtime and re-copies every file on resume (issue
// 17). Against a cas:// target the other documented ways out do not hold
// (measured on 26.04.6 with the sources at mode 000, every task cached):
//   copyAttributes = true  the cas provider reports a block's own mtime, so
//                          every file still differs and is re-copied;
//   overwrite 'sha256'     has to read every source byte to compare, which is
//                          the re-hash 4c forbids; under the lock it re-copies;
//   overwrite 'lenient'    files match on name and size, but each qc directory
//                          (a manifest pointer) differs in size and is re-copied.
// The Boolean false short-circuits PublishDir.shouldOverwrite with no I/O,
// which is what Nextflow itself does for a cached task under the legacy
// publishDir. The publish event still fires for every file.
//
// Not for the other runs: `again`, `fail` and `elsewhere` publish into
// coordinates `cold` already wrote, and must re-address them (assertion 2,
// browser assertion A1).
workflow.output.overwrite = false
